+# Upgrade — 2026-09-30
+
+Five production-readiness gates, plus the bugs they uncovered. Full write-up in
+**`NOTES-production.md`** — read that first; this file is just the index.
+
+## What changed
+
+| file | change |
+|---|---|
+| `arb/executor.py` | `min_profit` floor (gas + 25% buffer) so a run can never "profit" below its own gas cost; `v2_buy_cost_wei` — loan sized from leg 1's real `getAmountIn` cost; `best_leg` refuses venues with no router; revert-prediction notes name the right guard |
+| `arb/deployer.py` | `send_and_wait(..., submit_url=)` — private/MEV-protected broadcast that fails loudly instead of falling back to the public mempool; `GAS_PRICE_GWEI` override (default still 2 gwei vs BSC's ~0.05 market) |
+| `main.py` | `arb survey` (dry-run loop, JSONL evidence log); `--private`, `--min-profit-buffer` flags; gas→quote conversion and two-pass planning in `arb plan` / `arb run` |
+| `config.py` | Uniswap V3 routers added for **BSC, Ethereum and Base** (each verified on chain: bytecode, `factory()`, selector shape). BSC planning previously died with `v3=MISSING` |
+| `tests/test_math.py` | fixed the pytest collection collision (`1 passed, 1 error` → green); 10 new offline cases; `test_offline_maths_suite` bridge so pytest and `main.py selftest` agree |
+| `tests/test_fork.py` | **new** — 6 tests against a BNB Chain mainnet fork: profit on real pools, revert-without-moving-tokens, LOK trap, owner-only withdraw, flash-fee agreement |
+| `logs/arb_survey*.jsonl` | the evidence: `before_buy_cost_fix` (looked profitable) vs `after` (negative — the honest number) |
+| `docs/ev-private-memo.md` | public-vs-private submission decision and arithmetic |
+
+## Two ways to use this zip
+
+**A. Review the diff, then merge (recommended).**
+The zip keeps `.git`, so from the project root:
+
+```bash
+git status          # shows exactly which files the upgrade touched
+git diff --stat
+git diff arb/executor.py
+```
+
+Or apply the standalone patch to your own checkout:
+
+```bash
+git apply --check upgrade-2026-09-30.patch   # verify it applies
+git apply upgrade-2026-09-30.patch
+```
+
+**B. Replace your copy.** The tree is complete and self-contained apart from
+`.git/config` (stripped) and caches. Re-run the two suites after either route.
+
+Note: the patch is code and docs only. `logs/arb_survey*.jsonl` (the evidence
+`NOTES-production.md` cites) are gitignored, so they are in the full tree but not
+in the patch. `build/` is likewise not shipped — it regenerates on first compile.
+
+## Verify it works
+
+```bash
+python main.py selftest                    # 94/94 offline, no network
+python -m pytest tests/ -q                 # 2 passed
+python -m pytest tests/test_fork.py -q     # 6 passed (needs Foundry + archive RPC)
+```
+
+Fork tests need `anvil`. They probe for a BNB RPC that can serve archive state
+(`api.zan.top`, `bsc-mainnet.public.blastapi.io` work; publicnode does not) and
+skip cleanly if neither anvil nor a fork source is available.
+
+## Read before trading
+
+1. `NOTES-production.md` — findings, the cost floor table, the micro-drill runbook.
+2. `docs/ev-private-memo.md` — why `--private` is the default posture.
+
+**Headline: do not trade real size yet.** Not for code-quality reasons — the
+contract is now proven end to end against real mainnet state — but because the
+measured edge on the V2→V3 WBNB/USDT route is **negative** (−16 to −25 bps gross,
+−33 to −42 bps net, at 1 WBNB). The earlier "profitable" survey rows were a
+2×-fee modelling bug that is now fixed.
